# Minimal external library suppressions for ThreadSanitizer (P0-28 audited minimal set)
# Broad suppression race:libQt6Core.so has been eliminated and replaced with strictly scoped rules:
#
# 1. Target: Qt6 QTest internal watchdog thread data race during QTest teardown
#    Reason: Qt's test framework spawns an uninstrumented watchdog thread that accesses stack variables during exit.
#    Scope : Strictly scoped to libQt6Test test harness.
race:libQt6Test

# 2. Target: Qt6 QWaitCondition synchronization in precompiled Qt library
#    Reason: Precompiled distribution libQt6Core lacks TSan instrumentation for QWaitCondition futexes (used by QTest watchdog).
#    Scope : Strictly scoped to QWaitCondition symbol.
race:QWaitCondition

# 3. Target: Qt6 QTest internal watchdog thread leak at process exit
#    Reason: QTest watchdog thread is intentionally detached and not joined before exit by Qt test runner.
#    Scope : Strictly scoped to QThread::start (Desk32 production code uses std::thread exclusively).
thread:QThread::start

# 4. Target: PipeWire thread loop internal mutex unlock across threads
#    Reason: libpipewire-0.3 pw_thread_loop locks and unlocks mutex across internal loop/control threads by design.
#    Scope : Strictly scoped to third-party shared library libpipewire-0.3.so.
mutex:libpipewire-0.3.so

# 5. Target: Qt6 queued cross-thread event delivery in precompiled distribution libQt6Core
#    Reason: Precompiled distribution libQt6Core lacks TSan annotations for cross-thread event dispatching.
#    Scope : Strictly scoped to QObject::event symbol.
race:QObject::event
